<article class="env-definition" id="0EIP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EIP">Definition <span data-tag="0EIP">52.16.7</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EHC" data-tag="0EHC">52.16.1</a> let $(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ be an object of $\textit{Coh}(U, I\mathcal{O}_ U)$. We say <em>$(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ canonically extends to $X$</em> if the the inverse system </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \{ \widetilde{H^0(U, \mathcal{F}_ n)}\} _{n \geq 1}  \]
</div>
  <p> in $\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is pro-isomorphic to an object $(\mathcal{G}_ n)$ of $\textit{Coh}(X, I\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article>